# Markdown style for news rewrites

Use this file when the user asks for `@markdown-style.mdc`. It is the session house style.

Follow **both**:

1. `.cursor/rules/news-markdown-format.mdc` — compact `titles:` (3), description 140–160, `[tta_listen_btn]`, dateline, **elaborated multi-paragraph body** (blank lines; **≥5 paragraphs**; **≥300 words**, prefer **400+**), full source coverage, Footer SEO/meta, official/celebrity name checks.
2. `.cursor/rules/news-rewriting.mdc` — British English, `US` not `U.S.`, `per cent`, times as `9.00pm`, ordinal dates, no CJK, no outlet attribution, varied paragraph lengths, verify names online.

If the two conflict on skeleton, prefer **news-markdown-format.mdc**.

## Hard length + paragraph rules (STRICT)

- **Minimum 300 body words** — count before delivery. Prefer **350–450+**; long sources go longer.
- **Minimum 5 blank-line-separated paragraphs** — never a one-paragraph summary.
- One blank line after `[tta_listen_btn]`; blank line between every body paragraph.
- Do **not** join paragraphs with a single newline (Markdown merges them into one wall of text).
- Elaborate: unpack who/what/when/where, all figures, process, quotes (≤25 words), reactions — do not compress into a digest.

### Example (layout only — real pieces must hit the word floor)

```markdown
Verified: Name One; Name Two.

titles:

"Title one ends with a period."
"Title two ends with a period."
"Title three ends with a period." description: "140–160 characters…"
[tta_listen_btn]

10th August 2026 - (Hong Kong) Lede sentence on the dateline line.

Second paragraph — new idea, blank line above.

Third paragraph — blank line above.

Fourth paragraph — blank line above.

Fifth paragraph — blank line above (continue until ≥300–400 words and every source point is covered).

Footer SEO keyword: keyword Meta description: 140–160 characters…
Source: [HK01](https://www.hk01.com/article/<id>)
```
